		{
			"id": "eS_GN5vZgY0W8ge2q",
			"description": "Plasma Gun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The plasma gun is the Guard's and the Astartes' standard answer to power armour and light vehicles alike; fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts to Space Marine Battles depicts it killing power-armoured targets outright while carrying a real chance of cooking its own wielder, especially on older, less stable patterns - the origin of the tabletop and RPG \"gets hot\"/ overheat mechanic this entry represents mechanically as Malf 14 on the supercharged line.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed plasma anchor: 6dx4(3) burn ex, treated as the weapon's safe standard mode (no Malf risk) since it is already stated in the framework to kill Marines through power armour without needing to invoke overheating. Checked with the exact dice distribution, not just the average: Astartes power armour is torso DR 100; armour divisor (3) drops effective DR to 33, and 6dx4 averages 84, penetrating essentially every hit (99.9%), so it kills reliably as required. Against a Terminator's DR 200 (effective DR 66) it still penetrates 86% of hits, matching the framework's explicit statement that plasma \"penetrates Terminators more often than not.\" The supercharged mode (6dx5(3), Malf 14) bumps the multiplier one step further for harder targets (Mk X Gravis, multiple Terminators, light vehicles) at the cost of a real chance of the coil failing and burning the firer, matching the fiction's running theme of plasma weapons being feared by their own side almost as much as by the enemy.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "3200",
			"base_weight": "14 lb",
